{"slug":"smallest-and-largest","title":"Smallest and Largest","topic":"basics","difficulty":"easy","order":45,"tags":["arrays","loops","min-max"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Arrays: many values, one name","body":["An **array** (a *list* in Python, a *vector* in C++) stores many values under one name. The elements are numbered from **0**: an array of 5 numbers has the positions 0, 1, 2, 3 and 4, and the last one is at position `length - 1`. You read an element with square brackets: `a[0]` is the first.",{"code":"# Python\na = [5, 3, 8]\nprint(a[0], len(a))     # 5 3\nfor x in a:             # visits every element\n    print(x)\n\n// C++\nvector<long long> a = {5, 3, 8};\ncout << a[0] << \" \" << a.size();\nfor (long long x : a) { ... }\n\n// Java\nlong[] a = {5, 3, 8};\nSystem.out.println(a[0] + \" \" + a.length);\nfor (long x : a) { ... }"},"The starter code already reads the length `n` and the elements into `a`. To find the smallest and the largest, use the \"best so far\" idea again: start with the first element as both, and let every other element challenge them."]},"statement":["You are given `n` integers. Print the smallest and the largest of them, separated by a space."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`. The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["`smallest largest` on one line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"5\n3 -1 9 4 9\n","output":"-1 9\n","note":"The smallest is -1 and the largest is 9."},{"input":"1\n7\n","output":"7 7\n","note":"With one number it is both the smallest and the largest."}],"hints":["Start with `smallest = a[0]` and `largest = a[0]`.","Go through all elements. If one is smaller than `smallest`, it becomes the new smallest. Do the same for the largest.","Print the two values on one line, smallest first."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Both records start at the first element. Every element is compared with both records and replaces them when it is smaller or larger. After one pass the records are the minimum and the maximum."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1) besides the input.","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nsmallest = a[0]\nlargest = a[0]\nfor x in a:\n    if x < smallest:\n        smallest = x\n    if x > largest:\n        largest = x\nprint(smallest, largest)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    long long smallest = a[0];\n    long long largest = a[0];\n    for (long long x : a) {\n        if (x < smallest) {\n            smallest = x;\n        }\n        if (x > largest) {\n            largest = x;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << smallest << \" \" << largest << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        long smallest = a[0];\n        long largest = a[0];\n        for (long x : a) {\n            if (x < smallest) {\n                smallest = x;\n            }\n            if (x > largest) {\n                largest = x;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(smallest + \" \" + largest);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"1\n7\n","output":"7 7\n"},{"input":"5\n3 -1 9 4 9\n","output":"-1 9\n"},{"input":"3\n5 5 5\n","output":"5 5\n"},{"input":"3\n-3 -7 -1\n","output":"-7 -1\n"},{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"1 5\n"},{"input":"5\n5 4 3 2 1\n","output":"1 5\n"},{"input":"2\n1000000000 -1000000000\n","output":"-1000000000 1000000000\n"},{"input":"1000\n-925608989 827596000 573353421 -250639312 -81028795 -36137951 -942614117 453793530 135331430 508791602 305279281 849108625 -329018028 -792060318 89602488 944952605 257718077 626098033 -489825032 817422452 -204007988 698105408 665884187 681570093 -295356359 -419956003 757696360 -904612003 -17697118 -657145530 -716306625 847486687 -301751906 -950547860 -970733217 -213501904 -835626624 734711757 250068454 609902318 168333882 -557126485 -581470831 8110716 605507700 -28540115 609352719 -951269401 554863127 -224165978 -924932536 -908166734 287639666 860953310 -992141807 -187323933 -233789306 131750879 58121973 -809036666 448910296 -516382851 -790739085 219366870 12680882 -223054899 701548831 -84234557 -30919524 253315703 360680164 -344447241 -144315680 -343408341 -549214697 944108102 29201450 -177959568 -520656028 139087781 892153102 289095644 -401034162 -90879193 -550603293 800488538 -220366889 729125454 -368367423 -259568615 -592085374 -519643324 -438544858 257892251 803148818 -429089918 -83975383 548325408 -545064750 -833484982 -237923223 -78353148 -918595834 -377498259 -948980221 -776809485 -4576837 12357297 820901158 429795339 -440330968 -418427680 800341880 -767098433 -250827674 -654802847 542199462 830349784 901486393 -661963960 782380028 82636011 -574525223 -311538670 -161388233 -357733440 -951157891 808219793 37371602 -6682007 310370474 314207499 419235157 -987956131 -219877138 -810257468 -831348050 300415309 -538825302 -347864127 326528438 82349000